# Cross-platform determinism: Narvo verifies itself by hashing simulation state
# and diffing golden files. Neither may depend on the machine that produced them,
# so everything Git treats as text is stored and checked out with LF on every
# platform - Windows included.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Asset formats. Marking them binary keeps Git from touching their bytes and
# from trying to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
# Fonts joined the list with the glyph atlas (M3.34). `text=auto` already
# detects a TTF as binary by its NUL bytes and leaves it alone - checked, the
# blob and the file hash alike - but a 335 KiB asset that a committed SHA-256
# anchors should not rest on a heuristic.
*.ttf binary
